 1. What is an Agent?

An Agent is an AI system that can think, understand, decide, and take actions based on user input and backend data.

Unlike a normal LLM (which only generates text), an Agent can:

-- Understand natural language
-- Call tools / functions

(e.g., BigQuery, APIs, Databases, Cloud Functions)

-- Retrieve enterprise data

(files, BigQuery tables, GCS, databases)

--Maintain memory / context
-- Give accurate business answers
-- Perform tasks automatically

(reports, calculations, workflows)

Simple Example:

User: “Give me Bank of America’s profit trend for last 10 years.”
Agent:

Understand the question

Run BigQuery SQL

Format results into a chart/table

Explain insights conversationally

This is Agentic AI.

 2. How we build Agents in Google Cloud?

Google Cloud provides 3 ways to build an Agent:

 Option 1 — Vertex AI Agent Builder (GUI No-Code)

Used for: Chatbots, enterprise Q&A, customer service, document agents.

Steps:

Upload data → BigQuery / GCS / Websites

Create "Data Stores" and "Search Engines"

Create an Agent

Add Tools (Search, Functions)

Deploy → Web UI / API / Cloud Run

 Option 2 — Vertex AI Generative AI + Function Calling

Used for: Writing custom orchestration flows.

Steps:

Create a Vertex AI model endpoint

Define tools (Python functions / APIs)

Model calls tools with parameters

Return final aggregated answer

 Option 3 — ADK (Agent Developer Kit) (Recommended for your BofA project)

This is Google’s code-first framework for building production Agents.

With ADK, your agent can:

✔ Query BigQuery
✔ Call internal APIs
✔ Process files
✔ Run multiple steps intelligently
✔ Deploy to Cloud Run

Example ADK Agent flow:
User -> Agent -> Tool (BigQuery) -> Analysis -> Final Answer


This is the exact flow you are building for your Bank of America 10-year financial data agent.

 3. Prerequisites Before Building Agents (Very Important)

These setup steps must be ready before starting any Agent project.

 A. GCP Project Setup

A GCP Project

Billing Enabled

Vertex AI API Enabled

BigQuery API Enabled

Cloud Run API Enabled

 B. IAM / Service Accounts Required

Create a Service Account:

agent-sa@testadi-XXXX.iam.gserviceaccount.com


Assign roles:

Minimum Roles:

Vertex AI User

BigQuery Data Viewer

BigQuery Job User

Storage Object Viewer

Cloud Run Invoker

If using ADK:

Service Account User

Artifact Registry Reader

 C. Development Tools Required
If using ADK:

Python 3.10 or 3.11

Vertex AI SDK installed:

pip install google-cloud-aiplatform vertexai


ADK installed:

pip install google-cloud-aistudio

 D. Backend Data Prepared

For your use case:

Bank of America 10-year financial data

Stored in:
✔ BigQuery (best for querying)
✔ GCS (raw Excel files)

Agent needs access to:

bofa_financials.income_statement
bofa_financials.balance_sheet
bofa_financials.ratios

 E. Deployment Environment

You can deploy the agent to:

Cloud Run (serverless container) — recommended

VM (not recommended)

API Gateway + Cloud Functions (optional)

Web UI (Streamlit/Gradio/GCP UI)
